the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 10.

the events are:
    the train arrives at *a location*.
    I have a panic attack.
    the train catches fire.
    help arrives.
% composite/complex events:
    the driver stops the train.
    I alert the driver to an emergency.

the actions are:
    I press the alarm signal button.
   
the fluents are:
    the train is in *a location*.
    the next station is *a location*.
    there is an emergency.

the knowledge base new underground includes:

when the train catches fire
then there is an emergency.

when help arrives
then it is not the case that there is an emergency.

when the train arrives at a location
then the train is in the location.

when the train arrives at a location
then it is not the case that the next station is the location.

if there is an emergency at a time
then the driver stops the train from the time.

I alert the driver to an emergency from a time to an other time
if I press the alarm signal button from the time to the other time.

the driver stops the train from a time to an other time
if I alert the driver to an emergency from the time to the other time
and the train is in a station at the other time.

the driver stops the train from a first time to a second time
if I alert the driver to an emergency from the first time to an other time
and it is not the case that the train is in a station at the other time
and the next station is a location at the other time
and the train arrives at the location  to the second time.

it must not be true that
    I press the alarm signal button from a time 
    and it is not the case that there is an emergency at the time.

if I have a panic attack from a time
then the driver stops the train from an other time.

initially the next station is piccadilly circus.

the train catches fire from 2 to 3.
the train arrives at piccadilly circus from 4 to 5.
help arrives from 5 to 6.
I have a panic attack from 7 to 8.

    





